      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's another attempt at expanding the quest introduction:\n\nThe Whispering Hollows, where the moon's pale light weaves an eerie tapestry through the skeletal branches of the trees, have long been a place of whispered terrors and faded legends. For as long as anyone can remember, the Hollows have been a necromancer's whisper, a place where the veil between life and death is thin, and the whispered names of the ancient ones still linger in the flickering breeze. It's said that the Hollows were once a thriving monastery, where the Order of the Black Rose dwelled, their monks devoting themselves to the study of the arcane and the secrets of the dead. But as the ages passed, the Order was said to have made a pact with forces beyond mortal comprehension, and the Hollows were consumed by an eternal twilight, as if the very fabric of reality had been torn asunder. Few have ventured in and returned to tell the tale, but those who have speak of an existence in which time loses all meaning, and the very woods themselves seem to watch and wait, their ancient power seeping into the dreams of the sleeping. It's said that Elara, the old hermit, still dwells within these shadows",
